# diff
# Betaflight / SITL (SITL) 4.5.1
#
# AIR65 II FREESTYLE. BetaFPV's own factory tune for the Air65 II Freestyle,
# the 25000 kV variant on the bigger, softer GF1219S three blade. Optimised
# for low throttle torque and smooth cinematic flying rather than for a lap.
#
# PROVENANCE. Taken from "A65 II F_0702_Freestyle_GF 1219S_2026_6_0
# 20260515.txt", the CLI BetaFPV publishes for this aircraft at
# support.betafpv.com/hc/en-us/articles/54654422544409 (attachment
# 58300171193113). Betaflight 2026.6.0-alpha on a BETAFPVG473_V2 board;
# every PID, filter, TPA and idle value below is copied from it verbatim.
#
# THIS IS THE ODD ONE OUT and it is worth saying how. The two racing tunes
# hold their master multiplier below 100; the Freestyle leaves it at default
# and pushes pi_gain to 110, so it runs the HIGHEST gains of the three:
# roll P49 D35, pitch P56 D44. It is also the only one of the three on
# BETAFLIGHT rates rather than ACTUAL, at 846 deg/s roll and pitch with 0.30
# expo against the racers' dead linear 580. A freestyle whoop wants a stick
# that opens up hard at the top; a racing whoop wants one that does not.
#
# WHAT IS STILL WHOOP SPECIFIC, even at these higher gains:
#
#   * D is 71 percent of P against the 5 inch default's 89, and feedforward
#     is 35 against 120. A whoop needs almost no feedforward because it has
#     almost no inertia to overcome.
#   * d_max_gain is 20 against a default of 37. The D boost band is narrow
#     on all three of these tunes.
#   * tpa_breakpoint is 1240 against a default of 1350, with tpa_rate 60.
#     Even the gentle variant takes the gains off early, because 1S sag is
#     1S sag: 4.2 V open circuit falls to about 3.2 V under a punch, a 23
#     percent collapse where a 6S race pack loses 8.
#   * throttle_boost is 0. Every BetaFPV whoop dump sets it there; the 4.5.1
#     default is 5.
#   * dyn_idle_min_rpm 30, which is 3000 rpm, against a hover of 34,480.
#
# NO RATES, following configs/registry.js. BetaFPV ships this aircraft on
# BETAFLIGHT rates, rc_rate 110 / 110 / 120, expo 30, srate 74 / 74 / 64,
# which is 846 deg/s on roll and pitch and 667 on yaw. See configs/rates.js.
# To fly them approximately, set 846 max and 0.30 expo in Settings.
#
